WEBVTT

00:00:00.840 --> 00:00:02.260
<i>It's over!</i>

00:00:04.560 --> 00:00:05.310
<i>This is it!</i>

00:00:07.990 --> 00:00:10.210
<i>This is the last bit of strength I have saved...</i>

00:00:10.210 --> 00:00:12.310
<i>with everything I have behind it!</i>

00:00:12.510 --> 00:00:14.520
<i>Go!</i>

00:00:17.860 --> 00:00:19.070
It was stopped!

00:00:19.070 --> 00:00:20.930
Here comes the Bloody Cross!

00:00:20.930 --> 00:00:22.740
No! He can't dodge it!

00:00:23.020 --> 00:00:24.950
<i>Is it all over!?</i>

00:00:35.090 --> 00:00:36.710
<i>He's pushing it back!?</i>

00:00:37.280 --> 00:00:38.960
<i>It's not just his arm strength.</i>

00:00:39.220 --> 00:00:41.590
<i>His entire body... is behind it!</i>

00:00:56.830 --> 00:00:57.860
He's...

00:00:58.100 --> 00:01:00.430
He's down!

00:01:12.780 --> 00:01:14.310
He's down!

00:01:14.310 --> 00:01:16.170
A devastating attack!

00:01:16.920 --> 00:01:21.920
The prince's blade has been revived and skewers the champion into the mat!

00:01:24.620 --> 00:01:26.430
Get to a neutral corner!

00:01:26.880 --> 00:01:28.000
Well done!

00:01:28.000 --> 00:01:29.400
Now steady your breathing!

00:01:29.400 --> 00:01:31.430
Wait in the corner and try to relax!

00:01:33.340 --> 00:01:34.340
ONE

00:01:35.340 --> 00:01:36.340
TWO

00:01:37.610 --> 00:01:38.610
THREE

00:01:40.620 --> 00:01:41.620
FOUR

00:01:41.260 --> 00:01:43.190
<i>Forget about breathing.</i>

00:01:43.190 --> 00:01:45.220
<i>I can't even raise my arms anymore.</i>

00:01:45.220 --> 00:01:47.340
<i>My legs won't move either.</i>

00:01:47.340 --> 00:01:49.540
<i>I can't keep fighting like this,</i>

00:01:49.540 --> 00:01:50.830
<i>so please don't get up!</i>

00:01:51.110 --> 00:01:53.160
The champion doesn't move!

00:01:51.640 --> 00:01:52.640
FIVE

00:01:53.160 --> 00:01:55.130
Is he down for the count?

00:01:54.150 --> 00:01:55.150
SIX

00:01:55.130 --> 00:01:57.600
Don't get up, just stay down!

00:01:57.600 --> 00:02:00.130
Please, stay down!

00:02:00.820 --> 00:02:02.410
<i>I can't stop shaking.</i>

00:02:02.890 --> 00:02:04.670
<i>That was an amazing attack.</i>

00:02:05.380 --> 00:02:08.850
<i>A cross counter with his entire body weight behind it.</i>

00:02:08.850 --> 00:02:12.330
<i>If he had made even the slightest mistake, he would have been seriously hurt.</i>

00:02:12.330 --> 00:02:14.390
<i>And he threw it without any hesitation.</i>

00:02:15.210 --> 00:02:18.260
<i>You couldn't do that with ordinary determination and decisiveness.</i>

00:02:18.260 --> 00:02:21.400
<i>It's a punch you risk your soul on!</i>

00:02:21.950 --> 00:02:22.930
<i>Good work.</i>

00:02:22.930 --> 00:02:25.870
<i>You really did good throwing a Jolt Counter!</i>

00:02:25.870 --> 00:02:28.220
<i>The Jolt, thrown with your entire body,</i>

00:02:28.220 --> 00:02:31.040
<i>is the only punch that could overcome the Bloody Cross!</i>

00:02:31.430 --> 00:02:34.130
<i>That was a punch with Ichiro's entire body and soul behind it!</i>

00:02:34.130 --> 00:02:35.160
<i>He won't be able to get up!</i>

00:02:37.500 --> 00:02:38.500
SEVEN

00:02:40.420 --> 00:02:43.400
Whoa, the champion sits up!

00:02:42.710 --> 00:02:43.710
EIGHT

00:02:43.400 --> 00:02:45.010
Will he be able to stand!?

00:02:45.530 --> 00:02:47.160
<i>I-Impossible!</i>

00:02:47.160 --> 00:02:49.180
<i>Not after taking a Jolt Counter!</i>

00:02:50.220 --> 00:02:52.760
<i>That was all I had!</i>

00:02:52.760 --> 00:02:55.170
<i>My strongest attack!</i>

00:02:55.170 --> 00:02:55.940
<i>He can't get up!</i>

00:02:56.570 --> 00:02:58.480
<i>There's no way he can get up!</i>

00:03:01.440 --> 00:03:04.070
H-He's up!

00:03:05.210 --> 00:03:07.860
The challenger's jaw drops in shock!

00:03:09.140 --> 00:03:13.370
Now, will the champion be able to take his fighting pose!?

00:03:18.370 --> 00:03:20.200
Whoa!

00:03:20.200 --> 00:03:21.880
The champion...

00:03:25.260 --> 00:03:30.010
falls to the canvas like a puppet with its strings cut!

00:03:32.620 --> 00:03:34.690
The match is over!

00:03:34.690 --> 00:03:36.640
The championship changes hands!

00:03:37.030 --> 00:03:39.450
4 rounds, 1 minute and 34 seconds!

00:03:39.450 --> 00:03:43.290
The embers of a comeback ignite with a cross counter!

00:03:39.900 --> 00:03:43.290
All right! {jama: added, needs TLC}

00:03:43.290 --> 00:03:44.530
<i>Geez...</i>

00:03:44.530 --> 00:03:45.900
<i>talk about a close call.</i>

00:03:46.390 --> 00:03:49.590
A new OPBF Champion is crowned!

00:03:49.590 --> 00:03:52.450
His name is Miyata Ichiro!

00:03:54.910 --> 00:03:56.520
<i>What an embarrassment!</i>

00:03:56.520 --> 00:03:59.040
<i>After all that talk, this is what happens!?</i>

00:03:59.890 --> 00:04:02.000
<i>All that work for nothing!</i>

00:04:02.000 --> 00:04:04.170
<i>You can watch your own back from now on.</i>

00:04:04.740 --> 00:04:05.670
Ichiro!

00:04:05.670 --> 00:04:06.890
Ichiro-kun!

00:04:12.700 --> 00:04:13.750
Ichiro!

00:04:15.420 --> 00:04:16.800
How was it?

00:04:16.800 --> 00:04:18.370
Were you watching, Dad?

00:04:20.280 --> 00:04:22.880
I saw it, all right.

00:04:22.880 --> 00:04:24.190
You were splendid.

00:04:26.770 --> 00:04:27.900
Ichiro-kun!

00:04:27.900 --> 00:04:29.190
Your belt!

00:04:30.800 --> 00:04:31.700
Come on!

00:04:35.810 --> 00:04:37.190
Okay, let me off your shoulder. {This seems like a shorter line for the number of words}

00:04:37.980 --> 00:04:40.320
The champion has to look the part.

00:04:43.140 --> 00:04:48.090
Now the new champion is having his belt put on!

00:04:48.690 --> 00:04:52.090
He may be called a genius, but his champion road was still a harsh one!

00:04:52.570 --> 00:04:56.350
He took the long road, but he's finally gained the title!

00:05:01.780 --> 00:05:05.810
<i>After being hit so much and beaten up so badly...</i>

00:05:05.810 --> 00:05:08.110
<i>it's nothing to be proud of, but...</i>

00:05:08.840 --> 00:05:10.690
<i>there's a real meaning to this belt.</i>

00:05:11.430 --> 00:05:13.320
<i>A meaning to this victory.</i>

00:05:14.660 --> 00:05:16.080
<i>I can...</i>

00:05:17.240 --> 00:05:18.950
<i>hold my head up now!</i>

00:05:27.610 --> 00:05:30.100
He ends it with a guts pose.

00:05:30.100 --> 00:05:32.840
It's really like he stepped out of a painting.

00:05:32.840 --> 00:05:36.480
<i>He usually doesn't show his emotions, but...</i>

00:05:36.480 --> 00:05:39.480
<i>that just means it was that much of a hard-won victory.</i>

00:05:41.640 --> 00:05:43.390
Stop being mesmerized!

00:05:44.340 --> 00:05:47.060
B-But he's so cool!

00:05:47.060 --> 00:05:48.610
How about it, Japanese Champ?

00:05:48.610 --> 00:05:50.650
How does it feel to have your rival pass you?

00:05:51.190 --> 00:05:53.930
He's not my rival or anything.

00:05:57.240 --> 00:06:00.490
<i>I'll be back... when that gap is filled.</i>

00:06:01.680 --> 00:06:03.670
<i>More than closing the gap,</i>

00:06:03.670 --> 00:06:06.250
<i>he's suddenly gone way past me.</i>

00:06:07.190 --> 00:06:08.570
<i>That's right.</i>

00:06:08.570 --> 00:06:13.410
<i>I've always thought of Miyata-kun as being in the distance, as my goal.</i>

00:06:14.220 --> 00:06:17.550
<i>That's taken a clear shape today.</i>

00:06:18.500 --> 00:06:20.510
<i>The OPBF title!</i>

00:06:22.380 --> 00:06:25.520
<i>Looks like he's finally getting motivated.</i>

00:06:26.620 --> 00:06:28.810
<i>Now I can face you with pride.</i>

00:06:29.530 --> 00:06:30.830
<i>Bring it on whenever you're ready,</i>

00:06:30.830 --> 00:06:32.280
<i>Makunouchi Ippo!</i>

00:06:38.990 --> 00:06:40.840
That was a brilliant counter at the end!

00:06:40.840 --> 00:06:42.080
Any impressions from having won the title match?

00:06:42.080 --> 00:06:44.000
What's your next goal?

00:06:44.360 --> 00:06:46.570
Stop crowding him!

00:06:46.570 --> 00:06:48.750
The match just ended, so he's tired.

00:06:49.730 --> 00:06:51.900
You can schedule interviews later through the gym!

00:06:51.900 --> 00:06:52.760
No further comment!

00:06:57.140 --> 00:06:58.890
Can I mention one thing?

00:06:58.890 --> 00:07:00.010
Fujii-san?

00:07:00.610 --> 00:07:03.320
Arnie's manager, Mr. Sakaguchi,

00:07:03.320 --> 00:07:04.770
left alone.

00:07:05.520 --> 00:07:06.520
All by himself?

00:07:06.790 --> 00:07:10.090
He spat something about Arnie's commercial value having dried up.

00:07:11.010 --> 00:07:13.390
So he's abandoning him.

00:07:13.390 --> 00:07:15.840
Still, that's a hell of a way to show your true colors.

00:07:15.840 --> 00:07:18.820
Well, he was a shady customer to begin with.

00:07:59.210 --> 00:08:00.450
How...

00:08:02.030 --> 00:08:04.240
How were you able to withstand all that?

00:08:04.750 --> 00:08:07.370
I know for a fact that my punches aren't light.

00:08:08.210 --> 00:08:11.880
What was holding you up, after you took that much of a beating?

00:08:13.000 --> 00:08:14.710
I'm on the verge of losing my confidence.

00:08:15.320 --> 00:08:17.630
I can't go home like this.

00:08:18.480 --> 00:08:22.060
I want to hear the answer directly from you.

00:08:29.140 --> 00:08:32.140
I'm not sure if it'll satisfy you, but...

00:08:34.250 --> 00:08:35.940
I was just being stubborn.

00:08:37.340 --> 00:08:38.710
Stubborn?

00:08:38.710 --> 00:08:41.260
You were able to withstand all that just by being stubborn?

00:08:41.880 --> 00:08:44.950
Then you've got to be the most stubborn man alive!

00:08:46.500 --> 00:08:47.450
Maybe so.

00:08:51.760 --> 00:08:55.440
That answer is so simple and obvious that it makes sense.

00:08:56.880 --> 00:09:01.010
When I get back home, I'll be sure to tell them how stubborn the Japanese can be.

00:09:06.360 --> 00:09:08.950
And be careful, Ichiro Miyata.

00:09:09.580 --> 00:09:14.250
Mr. Sakaguchi will probably keep sending fighters after you for payback.

00:09:14.710 --> 00:09:16.270
They'll all be tough.

00:09:16.670 --> 00:09:18.260
I won't lose.

00:09:18.890 --> 00:09:21.280
I'm not giving up the belt I got from you.

00:09:22.340 --> 00:09:24.280
No matter who comes after it!

00:09:32.080 --> 00:09:34.010
Goodbye, Champ.

00:09:37.410 --> 00:09:38.440
Goodbye.

00:09:43.900 --> 00:09:47.010
<i>It took a long time to get here.</i>

00:09:48.380 --> 00:09:51.170
<i>But now I'm in a position comparable to him.</i>

00:09:52.070 --> 00:09:54.160
<i>I'll prepare myself to fight,</i>

00:09:54.160 --> 00:09:56.560
<i>and until the day we face each other again,</i>

00:09:56.920 --> 00:09:58.890
<i>I won't hand over the title to anyone.</i>

00:10:00.020 --> 00:10:02.220
<i>I'm going to face the best in Japan</i>

00:10:02.820 --> 00:10:05.230
<i>as the Oriental Pacific Region Champion!</i>

00:10:16.330 --> 00:10:18.690
Miyata was damn impressive!

00:10:18.690 --> 00:10:20.970
Being able to make a huge comeback after all that!

00:10:20.970 --> 00:10:23.300
That counter really gave me chills!

00:10:23.980 --> 00:10:26.340
Seeing it in person was really moving!

00:10:26.670 --> 00:10:29.910
It like, really gets the blood rushing to your muscles!

00:10:29.910 --> 00:10:33.100
Seeing something like that gets you pumped all right!

00:10:33.400 --> 00:10:35.720
It's hard to sit still!

00:10:36.720 --> 00:10:39.410
Guys without matches need to settle the hell down.

00:10:41.280 --> 00:10:42.360
Takamura-san?

00:10:44.060 --> 00:10:46.820
Because I'm up next!

00:10:49.210 --> 00:10:51.160
<i>The boxing world is at its boiling point.</i>

00:10:53.080 --> 00:10:57.120
<i>Makunouchi Ippo defends his title for the first time in an incredible match.</i>

00:10:58.400 --> 00:11:02.050
<i>Miyata Ichiro takes the Oriental Pacific Region Title.</i>

00:11:03.670 --> 00:11:04.940
<i>And...</i>

00:11:20.170 --> 00:11:22.590
<i>Still undefeated on the world stage,</i>

00:11:22.590 --> 00:11:24.940
<i>after a 10 round Jr. Middleweight Match...</i>

00:11:24.940 --> 00:11:28.240
<i>resulting in a third round victory against the 2nd ranked fighter in the world...</i>

00:11:28.440 --> 00:11:31.820
<i>Takamura Mamoru becomes a serious contender for the world title.</i>

00:11:32.090 --> 00:11:35.380
<i>The Japanese boxing world is getting more exciting all the time.</i>

00:11:35.380 --> 00:11:38.060
<i>And there's even more heat in the forecast for the future.</i>

00:11:38.060 --> 00:11:40.790
<i>Chief among them...</i>

00:11:40.790 --> 00:11:44.020
<i>The WBA World Featherweight Title Match.</i>

00:11:44.020 --> 00:11:48.010
<i>The champion, Ricardo Martinez vs. Date Eiji.</i>

00:11:48.740 --> 00:11:55.350
<i>The leader of the modern Japanese boxing scene is finally fighting for the world title.</i>

00:11:57.370 --> 00:11:58.910
Wow!

00:11:58.910 --> 00:12:00.400
Date-san's match was finalized!

00:12:00.760 --> 00:12:02.290
How about it, Ippo-kun?

00:12:02.290 --> 00:12:07.310
Any comment on the only man to beat you going into a world title match?

00:12:08.940 --> 00:12:11.660
I'm sure Date-san will win no matter who he fights!

00:12:11.660 --> 00:12:14.200
I mean, he's so strong!

00:12:16.970 --> 00:12:18.910
<i>Your fists are light.</i>

00:12:19.510 --> 00:12:22.420
<i>My fists are... light?</i>

00:12:22.970 --> 00:12:25.410
<i>I don't want to sound conceited, but...</i>

00:12:25.410 --> 00:12:27.140
<i>In these ten matches...</i>

00:12:27.140 --> 00:12:31.930
<i>my opponents weren't so weak that I could beat them with light punches.</i>

00:12:32.890 --> 00:12:34.930
<i>The meaning of "light" and "heavy" is different.</i>

00:12:35.890 --> 00:12:36.930
<i>The meaning?</i>

00:12:37.180 --> 00:12:41.060
<i>There's a lot of baggage that comes with the title of champion.</i>

00:12:41.060 --> 00:12:42.520
<i>The guys counting on you...</i>

00:12:42.520 --> 00:12:44.520
<i>The ones who've entrusted you with their dreams...</i>

00:12:44.520 --> 00:12:46.910
<i>The guys who are coming after you...</i>

00:12:46.910 --> 00:12:49.190
<i>All their wishes</i>

00:12:49.190 --> 00:12:50.950
<i>get burnt into your fists.</i>

00:12:52.250 --> 00:12:53.450
<i>Their wishes?</i>

00:12:53.650 --> 00:12:55.300
<i>The champion's fists,</i>

00:12:55.300 --> 00:12:57.940
<i>without exception, have that kind of weight to them.</i>

00:12:57.940 --> 00:13:01.170
<i>And out of all of 'em, the old man's fists are heavy as hell.</i>

00:13:02.170 --> 00:13:05.300
<i>And now, as part of the Champion Carnival,</i>

00:13:05.300 --> 00:13:09.670
<i>we will begin the 10 round Japanese Featherweight Title Match!</i>

00:13:10.500 --> 00:13:13.500
<i>In the red corner, from Nakadai Gym,</i>

00:13:13.500 --> 00:13:16.670
<i>weighing 125 and 1/4 pounds.</i>

00:13:16.670 --> 00:13:19.510
<i>The Japanese Featherweight Champion,</i>

00:13:19.510 --> 00:13:22.370
<i>Date Eiji!</i>

00:13:23.740 --> 00:13:27.090
<i>In the blue corner, from Kamogawa gym,</i>

00:13:27.090 --> 00:13:30.440
<i>weighing 124 and 1/2 pounds.</i>

00:13:30.440 --> 00:13:33.520
<i>The 1st ranked Japanese Featherweight,</i>

00:13:33.520 --> 00:13:37.190
<i>Makunouchi Ippo!</i>

00:13:41.220 --> 00:13:44.530
<i>And now, one of the most anticipated cards of the Champion Carnival begins,</i>

00:13:44.530 --> 00:13:47.180
<i>the Japanese Featherweight Title Match!</i>

00:13:47.180 --> 00:13:49.260
<i>Who is the strongest among Japan's Featherweights,</i>

00:13:49.260 --> 00:13:52.840
<i>Date or Makunouchi!?</i>

00:14:08.050 --> 00:14:09.520
<i>A right!</i>

00:14:09.730 --> 00:14:12.190
<i>Date's head is blasted backwards!</i>

00:14:17.580 --> 00:14:19.190
<i>I didn't feel...</i>

00:14:19.190 --> 00:14:20.110
<i>any feedback.</i>

00:14:30.340 --> 00:14:32.590
<i>H-He's twisting his neck...</i>

00:14:33.280 --> 00:14:35.590
<i>to kill the impact of the punch!</i>

00:14:37.460 --> 00:14:39.350
<i>A left from the champion!</i>

00:15:07.140 --> 00:15:10.040
<i>The champion's Heartbreak Shot!</i>

00:15:18.740 --> 00:15:20.910
<i>The challenger is wide open!</i>

00:15:21.810 --> 00:15:24.310
<i>It's over!</i>

00:15:24.310 --> 00:15:25.810
<i>Stop!</i>

00:15:41.230 --> 00:15:44.580
<i>T-The match has ended!</i>

00:15:44.580 --> 00:15:50.740
<i>The Japanese Featherweight Title Match has ended in the champion, Date Eiji's favor!</i>

00:15:50.740 --> 00:15:52.860
<i>He took the throne and still defends it at the age of 30!</i>

00:15:52.860 --> 00:15:55.300
<i>There's no competition for him nationally!</i>

00:15:55.300 --> 00:15:59.400
<i>Is the world title now in his sight!?</i>

00:16:00.700 --> 00:16:01.860
It'll be fine!

00:16:01.860 --> 00:16:02.770
He'll win!

00:16:02.770 --> 00:16:05.020
Date-san will definitely win!

00:16:06.010 --> 00:16:10.020
Can you say that knowing who his opponent is?

00:16:13.130 --> 00:16:16.220
WBA World Featherweight Champion,

00:16:16.220 --> 00:16:17.740
Ricardo Martinez.

00:16:18.610 --> 00:16:21.680
62 matches, 62 wins, 58 KO's!

00:16:21.680 --> 00:16:22.530
Undefeated!?

00:16:23.300 --> 00:16:24.870
What's with his record?

00:16:24.870 --> 00:16:26.040
It's perfect!

00:16:26.440 --> 00:16:28.730
He's a big Mexican hero.

00:16:28.730 --> 00:16:33.540
Even the guys who don't know the president's name over there know who Ricardo is.

00:16:33.820 --> 00:16:38.550
And Date-san happens to be among those 62 casualties.

00:16:40.530 --> 00:16:41.870
That's right.

00:16:41.870 --> 00:16:44.510
Date-san lost to this champion once.

00:16:57.900 --> 00:17:01.800
Even though it's Date-san, I'm still pretty worried.

00:17:01.800 --> 00:17:06.620
I mean, he's a super champion who's defended the world title 17 times.

00:17:06.620 --> 00:17:07.800
"He'll win!"

00:17:07.800 --> 00:17:09.930
"Date-san will definitely win!"

00:17:09.930 --> 00:17:11.750
Not gonna say that again?

00:17:12.000 --> 00:17:14.610
W-Well, I want to.

00:17:14.610 --> 00:17:16.890
Date-san is really strong,

00:17:16.890 --> 00:17:19.260
so I can't imagine him losing, but...

00:17:21.270 --> 00:17:25.240
But you can't imagine the champion losing either, right?

00:17:25.240 --> 00:17:26.010
Yes. {jama: added}

00:17:26.480 --> 00:17:30.660
The world titles that Japan acknowledges are the WBC and WBA.

00:17:30.660 --> 00:17:36.020
If he avoided Ricardo and went after the WBC, his chances might be better,

00:17:36.020 --> 00:17:41.230
but old man Date purposely went after the WBA champion that he'd already lost to once before.

00:17:41.230 --> 00:17:42.060
No,

00:17:42.060 --> 00:17:44.530
it might be more accurate to say he's been chasing after Ricardo

00:17:44.530 --> 00:17:46.530
ever since he lost to him seven years ago.

00:17:47.060 --> 00:17:49.380
Chasing after him?

00:17:49.380 --> 00:17:51.930
After all, Date-san is already 30.

00:17:52.450 --> 00:17:55.070
Given his age, this is probably his last chance.

00:17:55.070 --> 00:17:56.810
That's pretty damn cool.

00:17:56.810 --> 00:18:00.420
Going after the only guy to give you a black mark.

00:18:00.420 --> 00:18:01.670
That's true,

00:18:01.670 --> 00:18:03.220
and it's just like Date-san to do that.

00:18:03.690 --> 00:18:06.420
He might seem to be at a disadvantage when you think about it.

00:18:06.420 --> 00:18:08.720
But this is how I see it.

00:18:09.270 --> 00:18:12.230
The old man thinks he can win.

00:18:13.280 --> 00:18:14.230
He does?

00:18:14.550 --> 00:18:18.720
Since his match with you, he's gotten even stronger.

00:18:18.720 --> 00:18:21.570
He's been building his skills and strengthening his confidence.

00:18:21.570 --> 00:18:25.240
That's why he was willing to slam down a challenge against Ricardo.

00:18:25.610 --> 00:18:27.930
Y-You're right!

00:18:27.930 --> 00:18:30.460
He wouldn't have challenged him if he didn't think he could win!

00:18:30.940 --> 00:18:32.950
If Date-san wins, he'll be...

00:18:34.450 --> 00:18:35.870
the world champion!

00:18:40.040 --> 00:18:42.300
T-This is incredible!

00:18:42.300 --> 00:18:43.470
It's amazing, right!?

00:18:43.470 --> 00:18:45.990
The person who beat me will be the world champion!

00:18:45.990 --> 00:18:47.290
The person who beat me!

00:18:47.290 --> 00:18:49.350
That's a weird thing to be proud of.

00:18:49.870 --> 00:18:53.850
Well, being world champion is considered the strongest man in the world, right?

00:18:55.290 --> 00:18:57.790
The strongest man in the world...

00:18:57.790 --> 00:18:59.170
I wonder what he's like?

00:18:59.170 --> 00:19:01.120
I can't even imagine it!

00:19:01.120 --> 00:19:03.490
How about finding out firsthand?

00:19:04.650 --> 00:19:05.990
Coach...

00:19:06.240 --> 00:19:09.490
What do you mean by that?

00:19:09.490 --> 00:19:14.490
The strongest man in the world, Ricardo Martinez, will be arriving in Japan soon.

00:19:15.090 --> 00:19:16.510
And...

00:19:16.510 --> 00:19:19.540
he's requested a sparring partner.

00:19:19.880 --> 00:19:21.340
O-Okay.

00:19:21.340 --> 00:19:25.130
He's requested the Japanese Featherweight Champion.

00:19:25.570 --> 00:19:26.950
Oh,

00:19:26.950 --> 00:19:28.700
the Japanese Champion.

00:19:35.240 --> 00:19:37.810
W-Wait, me?

00:19:37.810 --> 00:19:39.770
I'm going to fight the world champion!?

00:19:40.450 --> 00:19:43.270
I know you don't stand a chance.

00:19:43.790 --> 00:19:46.490
I don't even expect you to put on a good showing, but...

00:19:46.490 --> 00:19:51.030
it'd be good for you to see what the world class fighers are like firsthand.

00:19:51.590 --> 00:19:52.680
How about it?

00:19:52.680 --> 00:19:53.640
Are you up for it?

00:19:55.200 --> 00:19:56.310
Me...

00:19:56.310 --> 00:19:57.990
against the world champion.

00:20:03.470 --> 00:20:04.440
<i>Me...</i>

00:20:12.210 --> 00:20:13.390
I'll do it!

00:20:13.390 --> 00:20:14.560
I want to do it!

00:20:15.990 --> 00:20:18.330
I'll tell them you agreed then.

00:20:18.330 --> 00:20:19.850
Please do!

00:20:21.550 --> 00:20:23.040
<i>I might be able to...</i>

00:20:23.040 --> 00:20:25.140
<i>find out a habit the champion has,</i>

00:20:25.140 --> 00:20:27.820
<i>or something else that might help Date-san.</i>

00:20:28.660 --> 00:20:30.710
<i>But more than that, I want to see...</i>

00:20:30.710 --> 00:20:34.330
<i>how I would do against him with my current strength...</i>

00:20:35.250 --> 00:20:36.380
<i>if I fight him seriously!</i>
